#, no-wrap
msgid "How to minimize the amount of usage spent processing and running a job."
msgstr "ジョブの処理と実行に費やす使用量を最小化する方法。"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Minimize job run time"
msgstr "ジョブの実行時間を最小化する"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Minimize job run time {#minimize-job-run-time}"
msgstr "ジョブの実行時間を最小化する {#minimize-job-run-time}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "There are several ways you can limit the amount of time spent processing and running a job:\n"
msgstr "ジョブの処理と実行に費やす時間を制限する方法はいくつかあります：\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run only as many shots as you need: A job's QPU consumption (and therefore, its cost) scales with the number of shots. Therefore, you can manage your cost by running only as many shots as you need. For Estimator jobs, lower precision typically requires more shots and therefore a longer execution time.\n"
msgstr "**必要なショット数だけを実行する**：ジョブのQPU消費量（およびそのコスト）はショット数に比例してスケールします。そのため、必要なショット数だけを実行することでコストを管理できます。Estimator ジョブでは、精度を低くすると一般的にショット数が増え、実行時間も長くなります。\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "Set limits on execution time:  You can limit how long each job, batch, or session runs.  For details, see [Maximum execution time for Qiskit Runtime workloads](max-execution-time).\n"
msgid "Set limits on execution time:  You can limit how long each job, batch, or session runs.  For details, see the [Maximum execution time](/guides/max-execution-time) guide.\n"
msgstr "**実行時間に制限を設ける**：各ジョブ、バッチ、またはセッションの実行時間を制限できます。詳細については、[Qiskit Runtime ワークロードの最大実行時間](max-execution-time)を参照してください。\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use only the necessary settings for error suppression and error mitigation, because higher values can cause your jobs to run longer. See [Introduction to options](/guides/runtime-options-overview), [Configure error suppression](/guides/error-mitigation-and-suppression-techniques), and [Configure error mitigation](error-mitigation-and-suppression-techniques) for details.\n"
msgstr "**エラー抑制とエラー軽減に必要な設定のみを使用する**：値を高く設定するとジョブの実行時間が長くなる場合があります。詳細については、[オプションの概要](/guides/runtime-options-overview)、[エラー抑制の設定](/guides/error-mitigation-and-suppression-techniques)、および[エラー軽減の設定](error-mitigation-and-suppression-techniques)を参照してください。\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"- If you are running multiple jobs that contain the same (likely parameterized) circuits and are using an error mitigation method that requires noise models, such as PEA and PEC, consider using `NoiseLearner`. With this helper program, you can learn the noise model of a circuit once and reuse the model in subsequent Estimator queries. Note that a noise model becomes stale after a certain time, so this is only practical if there is no long delay between jobs (for example, within a session). See [Noise learning helper\n"
"](/guides/noise-learning) for more details.\n"
msgstr ""

